From 28888d89305f3511c0b18633e162a990e96c8994 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stella Reine <stella@styna.net>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:33:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] windows.ui.xaml: Implement a XAML Islands hosting subset.

Add WindowsXamlManager, DesktopWindowXamlSource with
IDesktopWindowXamlSourceNative(2), and XamlReader.Load with an element
tree for Grid, StackPanel, Border, TextBlock, ProgressBar, SwapChainPanel,
Viewbox, Path and Rectangle. Layout follows XAML measure/arrange rules and
content is rendered with an anti-aliased software rasterizer into the
bridge window.

The bridge stays on top of host GDI painting and ignores a layered style
set by the host, matching composition-presented islands. SwapChainPanel
accepts a swapchain but does not composite it yet.

The interface definitions in xaml_abi.idl are generated from Windows
metadata; interface types this module does not implement are lowered to
IInspectable with identical ABI.

This is what the FiveM updater needs (UpdaterUI.cpp).
